plan_ops.py | 233 | \u2713 VERIFIED |\\n| `artifact_read` | backlog_core/server.py | 3522 | \u2713 VERIFIED |\\n| `backlog_get_ready_sam_tasks` | backlog_core/server.py | 3606 | \u2713 VERIFIED |\\n\\n### Field Trimming on `backlog_get_ready_sam_tasks` (Verified)\\n\\nCode at backlog_core/operations.py:5127-5134 trims each ready task to exactly 5 fields: `id`, `name`, `agent`, `skills`, `issue_number`. Unbounded only by count, not document size. The artifact's Resolved Questions correction (revision 1 was wrong, revision 2 is right) is accurate.\\n\\n### `sam_schema/` Independence (Verified)\\n\\n- No token-budget constant in sam_schema/ (git grep across directory confirmed)\\n- No imports of progressive_markdown in sam_schema/ (git grep confirmed)\\n\\n### `ProgressiveMarkdownNavigator` Scope (Verified)\\n\\nnavigator.py:29-37 documents it operates on \\\"a parsed markdown document\\\" with \\\"document map, section navigation, code block viewing, link inventory, and search.\\\" Cannot address flat Pydantic record types (Task, Plan are not heading trees).\\n\\n### Three Independent Token-Budget Implementations (Verified)\\n\\nThe artifact correctly identifies three locations with competing token-budget definitions:\\n\\n1. **backlog_core/server.py:226-231** \u2014 _LIST_TOKEN_BUDGET (4_400) and _VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET (4_000)\\n2. **sam_schema/server_plan_ops.py:55** \u2014 _TOKEN_BUDGET (4_400)\\n3. **progressive_markdown/models.py:14-16** \u2014 _DEFAULT_BUDGET (9_500 or env-derived)\\n\\nNote: progressive_markdown/list_navigator.py:41's `TOKEN_BUDGET` is an alias to _DEFAULT_BUDGET (the shared constant), not a competing implementation. The architecture uses one shared engine constant (_DEFAULT_BUDGET) and two competing reimplementations in application code (backlog_core's two, sam_schema's one).\\n\\n### `paginate_results` as Drop-in Replacement (Verified)\\n\\nprogressive_markdown/list_navigator.py:539 explicitly documented as \\\"Drop-in shim: paginate_results (replaces _paginate_results in server.py)\\\".\\n\\n### Plan & Task Documentation Silence on Size (Verified)\\n\\nBoth sam_schema/core/models.py:135 (Task) and :279 (Plan) docstrings describe field structure only. No language about response size, document bounds, or content limits.\\n\\n### Output-Schema Headroom (Verified)\\n\\n**Artifact claim:** 12,773 tokens used; 227 tokens headroom on 13,000 ceiling\\n**Measurement (7e6381259):** 12,773 tokens (excluding profile_list/profile_load per test filter at line 17)\\n**Headroom:** 227 tokens\\n**Status:** \u2713 VERIFIED\\n\\nThe EXCLUDED_TOOLS set (profile_list, profile_load) totals 24 tokens and is filtered out of the assertion by test_tool_output_schemas.py:56. The 13,000-token ceiling governs only the 12,773-token sum.\\n\\n### Adjacent Stale Measurement (Documented)\\n\\nTest comment at test_tool_output_schemas.py:44 states \\\"Measured at 1,904 tokens\\\" for backlog_view. Actual measurement on 7e6381259: 1,706 tokens. The comment is stale and should be corrected to 1,706.\\n</details>\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-20T10:31:40.871934Z</sub>\\n\\n**STATUS: VERIFIED \u2014 All nine major claims confirmed accurate on 7e6381259.**\\n\\n### Surface Locations (Verified)\\n\\nAll five unbounded read surfaces located precisely as cited:\\n\\n| Surface | Location | Line |\\n|---------|----------|------|\\n| `sam_plan(action=\\\"read\\\")` | sam_schema/server.py | 95 |\\n| `sam_task(action=\\\"read\\\")` | sam_schema/server.py | 167 |\\n| `sam_plan(action=\\\"ready\\\")` | sam_schema/server_plan_ops.py | 233 |\\n| `artifact_read` | backlog_core/server.py | 3522 |\\n| `backlog_get_ready_sam_tasks` | backlog_core/server.py | 3606 |\\n\\n### Field Trimming on `backlog_get_ready_sam_tasks` (Verified)\\n\\nCode at backlog_core/operations.py:5127-5134 trims each ready task to exactly 5 fields: `id`, `name`, `agent`, `skills`, `issue_number`. Unbounded only by count, not document size. The artifact's Resolved Questions correction (revision 1 incorrect, revision 2 correct) is accurate.\\n\\n### `sam_schema/` Independence (Verified)\\n\\n- No token-budget constant in sam_schema/ (git grep across directory confirmed)\\n- No imports of progressive_markdown in sam_schema/ (git grep confirmed)\\n\\n### `ProgressiveMarkdownNavigator` Scope (Verified)\\n\\nnavigator.py:29-37 operates on \\\"a parsed markdown document\\\" with heading-tree navigation. Cannot address flat Pydantic record types (Task, Plan).\\n\\n### Three Independent Token-Budget Implementations (Verified)\\n\\nThe artifact correctly identifies three competing implementations:\\n\\n1. **backlog_core/server.py:226** \u2014 `_LIST_TOKEN_BUDGET` (4_400)\\n2. **backlog_core/server.py:231** \u2014 `_VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET` (4_000)\\n3. **sam_schema/server_plan_ops.py:55** \u2014 `_TOKEN_BUDGET` (4_400)\\n\\nNote: progressive_markdown/list_navigator.py:41's `TOKEN_BUDGET` is an alias to `_DEFAULT_BUDGET`, the shared engine constant, not a competing implementation. The architecture has one shared engine constant and three competing application-level reimplementations.\\n\\n### `paginate_results` as Drop-in Replacement (Verified)\\n\\nprogressive_markdown/list_navigator.py:539 explicitly documented: \\\"Drop-in shim: paginate_results (replaces _paginate_results in server.py)\\\".\\n\\n### Plan & Task Documentation Silence on Size (Verified)\\n\\nBoth sam_schema/core/models.py:135 (Task) and :279 (Plan) docstrings describe field structure only. No language about response size, document bounds, or content limits.\\n\\n### Output-Schema Headroom (Verified)\\n\\n**Artifact claim:** 12,773 tokens used; 227 tokens headroom on 13,000 ceiling  \\n**Measurement:** 12,773 tokens (excluding EXCLUDED_TOOLS) | headroom: 227 tokens\\n\\nThe exclusion set (profile_list, profile_load) totals 24 tokens and is filtered out of the assertion by test_tool_output_schemas.py:56 via `EXCLUDED_TOOLS = {\\\"profile_list\\\", \\\"profile_load\\\"}` with comment \\\"different ownership, out of scope\\\". The 13,000-token ceiling governs the 12,773-token sum of included tools only.\\n\\n### Stale Measurement in Test Comment (Documented)\\n\\ntest_tool_output_schemas.py:44 states backlog_view schema is \\\"Measured at 1,904 tokens\\\". Actual measurement on 7e6381259: 1,706 tokens. Comment is stale by 198 tokens and should be corrected.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-20T10:44:44.862331Z</sub>\\n\\n## Expanded Scope Verification (7e6381259)\\n\\n**Second unbounded path (ledger read functions):** VERIFIED.\\n- `dh_core/ledger/transitions.py::read` at line 927 (function definition) and `dh_core/ledger/queries.py::ready` at line 134 (function definition) form a second unbounded path.\\n- Verified: `ready` defaults `full=True` at line 134 (parameter: `full: bool = True`).\\n- `LedgerReadyResult` is documented at `sam_schema/core/models.py:617` (class definition).\\n- SAM CLI `plan ready` command at line 1399 calls `ledger.ready(conn, _plan_of(plan_address))` with NO budget parameter.\\n- SAM CLI `plan read` command at line 1583 (function definition; claim stated line 1605 is REFUTED\u2014line 1605 is within the function body, not the definition).\\n\\n**Subagent contract requirement:** VERIFIED (reference only).\\n- `skills/subagent-contract/SKILL.md` at line 90 references `plan read --address P/T --attempt N` as part of the contract.\\n\\n**Eight agent/skill files assume full-record shape:** SPOT-VERIFIED.\\n- Spot-checked: `agents/swarm-task-planner.md:355` reads plan via `mcp__plugin_dh_sam__sam_plan(\u2026, \\\"read\\\")`.\\n- Spot-checked: `agents/plan-validator.md:89` and line 475-478 call `sam_plan(action='read')` without budget.\\n- Spot-checked: All checked references call read operations that return full documents, not compact forms.\\n- Full verification of all eight files deferred pending time availability.\\n\\n**Component architecture contradiction:** VERIFIED.\\n- Line 81: \\\"#3058\\\" statement reads: \\\"Routing plan and task reads through progressive_markdown remains tracked by #3058.\\\"\\n- Line 151: \\\"#3078\\\" statement reads: \\\"Tracked in #3078\\\" (referring to artifact_read delivery via progressive_markdown).\\n- **Contradiction**: Line 81 assigns read-routing work to #3058; line 151 assigns artifact_read specifically to #3078.\\n- **Verdict**: Different issue numbers stated for the same work (progressive_markdown delivery of content reads).\\n\\n**Previously verified claim (operations.py dead code):** CONFIRMED.\\n- `dh_core/operations.py:477-515` \u2014 `full` parameter appears only in function signature and docstring.\\n- No branch on `full` exists in the function body; parameter is ignored. Verified: dead code on content-store path.\\n\\n**Character count discrepancy:** REPORTED.\\n- Impact Radius section reported at ~69,772 characters; stored entry is 33,869 characters \u2014 a gap of ~35,903 characters.\\n- No re-verification attempted; issue noted as factual observation.\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nNine of ten claims verified or refuted with evidence:\\n- 7 verified as stated (two functions, default parameter, documentation location, command calls, contradiction)\\n- 1 refuted (plan read line number: claimed 1605, actual 1583)\\n- 2 partially verified pending full sweep (eight files claim requires checking all eight files; one already confirmed as dead code)\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-21T09:23:08.906287Z</sub>\\n\\n## Correction \u2014 2026-09-21: the output-schema headroom claim is about the wrong server\\n\\n**Recorded, and wrong:** \\\"Output-Schema Headroom (Verified) \u2014 12,773 tokens used; 227 tokens headroom\\\" cited as a HIGH-risk gate constraining `sam_plan`/`sam_task` schema growth in this item's Impact Radius.\\n\\n**Falsification:** `tests/test_tool_output_schemas.py:15` reads `from backlog_core.server import mcp`. The test measures the **backlog_core** server's 43 tools. `sam_plan` and `sam_task` are declared on the sibling **sam_schema** server (`sam_schema/server.py:95`, `:167`) and are not in that measurement. `grep -c \\\"sam_schema\\\\|sam_plan\\\\|sam_task\\\"` over the test returns 3 \u2014 all inside comments, none a measurement.\\n\\n**What the file actually says.** Line 21 is a cautionary comment, not a measurement: \\\"consolidated tool's outputSchema alone costs 8,758 tokens (sam_plan)\\\". It names the sibling server as the failure mode this test exists to prevent *in backlog_core*.\\n\\n**Corrected reading.** The 227-token headroom is backlog_core's and does not constrain this item. The real exposure is the inverse: `sam_plan`'s output schema costs 8,758 tokens and **no test covers the sam_schema server's output schemas at all**. Any response-shape change this item makes to `sam_plan` or `sam_task` is unguarded.\\n\\n**Consequence for scope.** Adding a schema ceiling test for the sam_schema server belongs in this item's acceptance criteria, because this item changes exactly those schemas and nothing currently measures them.\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-20T10:08:28.927871Z</sub>\\n\\n<details><summary>struck: 2026-09-20T11:05:43.435411Z \u2014 Fix decision line format for gate parsing; strike baseline snapshot</summary>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: refactor: route plan, task, and artifact reads through the markdown engine\\nDate: 2026-09-20\\nGoal: Every plan read, task read, artifact content read, and ready-task listing returns a usable response within the token budget, with the whole of a large document reachable across successive calls.\\nConditions:\\n1. The affected read surfaces are identified with their locations | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. Whether any of the four surfaces applies a token budget today | Status: AVAILABLE\\n3. The budget constant to apply, and how it resolves | Status: AVAILABLE\\n4. The normative behaviour required of an over-budget response | Status: AVAILABLE\\n5. Whether any prior implementation of this issue exists | Status: AVAILABLE\\n6. Output-schema headroom a