 entirely\\\" and states that artifact_read() returns raw content with no parsing, navigation or pagination. Both appear to own the same surface. Either #3078 is a subset of this issue, or one of the two drops artifact reads from its scope. Two plans touching artifact_read would collide the way #3057 and #3059 do on disclosure_handler.py. The owner decides.\\n\\nThis is the pre-swarm baseline. The rtica-assessor's final pass in finalize.md supersedes it.\\n</details>\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-20T10:57:33.671590Z</sub>\\n\\n<details><summary>struck: 2026-09-20T11:05:43.435411Z \u2014 Fix decision line format for gate parsing; strike baseline snapshot</summary>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final Assessment: refactor: route plan, task, and artifact reads through the markdown engine\\nDate: 2026-09-20 (final pass supersedes baseline)\\nGoal: Every plan read, task read, artifact content read, and ready-task listing returns a usable response within the token budget, with the whole of a large document reachable across successive calls.\\n\\n## Baseline Restatement\\n\\nPre-swarm baseline (2026-09-20 10:25 UTC) identified 11 conditions: 6 AVAILABLE, 4 DERIVABLE, 1 MISSING. Decision: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS.\\n\\n## Scope Expansion Assessment\\n\\nImpact Radius section confirms nine systems outside the five starting surfaces:\\n\\n1. Ledger-backed read/ready code paths (`dh_core/ledger/transitions.py::read`, `dh_core/ledger/queries.py::ready`) \u2014 second unbounded family outside sam_schema's import graph\\n2. Pre-existing defect in `dh_core/operations.py::get_ready_tasks` \u2014 `full` parameter is dead code on content-store branch (classified as defect, not MISSING condition)\\n3. Eight agent/skill prompt-contract files assuming full-record shape (identified and spot-verified)\\n4. Three-way divergent token-budget implementations requiring reconciliation (identified at three locations)\\n5. Documentation contradiction in `docs/component-architecture.md` (confirmed: lines 81 vs 145-151 a